Reduce SM80 static-FP8 verifier register pressure without changing cache layout.

The long-context partial kernel is limited to roughly 12.5% theoretical occupancy:
its FP32 [BLOCK_M, D] running output pushes the generated q=8 kernel to 255 registers
per thread and a 96-byte local frame.  Static E4M3 KV is already lossy and the
partial output is stored for a later cross-segment reduction, so retain FP32 for
scores, maxima and normalizers while rounding only the per-tile running output to
FP16.  The explicit dequantized-reference suite stays far below its existing error
budget, including q=64, mixed requests and a high physical block id.

The production 896-token page is an integral number of 32-token kernel tiles.  In
that exact static-FP8 case every tile has one block id, so load it once and build a
scalar page base rather than carrying 32 identical block IDs and two 2-D page-base
expressions.  Other quantization modes and non-integral page geometries retain the
original path.

Apply after spec-decode-fp8-lut-sm80.patch.

